## Context

Bridge dream lag without a memory bus. Pin publication G and current accepted branch corpus C; use unchanged ranked bodies from G, current withdrawals from C, and changed/unprocessed revisions as the recent supplement.

Design baseline: v6, merged by PR #903. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Library/CLI publication from 0910; branch corpus and snapshot from 0920; budget profile and manifest contract.

## Actions

1. Implement lightweight static-order filtering and refill only within the published available set. Evaluate basic scope in the consuming checkout; preserve unknown labels.
2. Derive provisional status from processed UUID/revisions, not another stored lifecycle flag. Bound the recent supplement; overflow remains searchable.
3. Apply withdrawal before budget selection; exclude stale orientation revisions even if their replacement is unavailable or does not fit.
4. Use ordinary Git integration and optimistic expected revisions. No global/distributed lock, cross-branch exchange or uncommitted global overlay.

## Test

Write during compilation, then load: the new committed revision remains recent. Retract an orientation entry with unavailable replacement: old advice is absent. Two branches add independent bodies then integrate: both survive. Conflicting same-UUID edits are reported, never latest-timestamp-wins.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v6, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Own-branch committed memories are eligible before PR merge and dreaming.
- [ ] Loader respects orientation/recent caps and avoids duplicate UUID exposure.
- [ ] Relocation/unknown context works without model or network.
